  "text": "Designing a reliable file backup system requires a shift in mindset from simply \"copying files\" to implementing a **data resilience strategy**. The goal is not just to have a copy of your data, but to ensure that you can recover that data quickly and completely regardless of the failure scenario (hardware crash, ransomware, or natural disaster).\n\nHere is a comprehensive guide to designing a reliable file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Core Strategy: The 3-2-1 Rule\nBefore diving into technical details, adhere to the industry-standard **3-2-1 Backup Rule**:\n*   **3** copies",
